{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "16", "M": "45", "S": "07"}}, "news": [{"title": "New fire-safety norms may shrink usable space in Rajasthan buildings", "para": "Rajasthan's local government has implemented new fire-safety rules for buildings.  These regulations require a minimum of two staircases in many structures. Architects warn this change will reduce usable carpet and built-up area.  The new norms apply to buildings requiring a fire no-objection certificate.  Builders may face challenges in planning and construction due to these requirements.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/new-fire-safety-regulations-to-impact-building-designs-in-rajasthan/132785313?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-649475/132785313.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Bhubaneswar: BMC to seal 112 residential buildings for operating as commercial centres illegally", "para": "Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation is sealing 112 residential buildings operating commercially.  A further survey will identify more such illegal commercial structures next month.  This action follows Supreme Court observations on building use deviations.  BMC aims to increase revenue by assessing commercial holding taxes accurately.  A private agency will help identify and classify new unassessed buildings.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/bmc-to-seal-112-residential-buildings-for-illegal-commercial-use-in-bhubaneswar/132785346?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-340216/132785346.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Rajkot civic body announces two-month interest waiver on property, water tax dues", "para": "Rajkot Municipal Corporation offers a two-month interest waiver on pending tax dues. This initiative aims to encourage taxpayers to clear outstanding amounts promptly. The civic body expects over 56,000 taxpayers to benefit from this scheme. This waiver is intended to help meet the corporation's tax collection targets. Timely payments will contribute to the city's ongoing development projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/rajkot-municipal-corporation-offers-interest-waiver-on-property-and-water-tax-dues/132785331?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-514842/132785331.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}